# Arm migration (agent/gcp-multitopology-v3): narrow exceptions so the
# corrected Cycle B2 corpus can be committed through Git LFS without
# exposing cycle-a/cycle-b (old) or any future cycle's shards. Raw scenario
# .npz arrays stay ignored everywhere, including cycle-b2 -- those are
# preserved as compressed archives under artifacts/migration/ instead (see
# .gitattributes and docs/ARM_MIGRATION.md).
!data/learning-v2/cycle-b2/tensors/**/*.safetensors
!data/learning-v2/cycle-b2/tensors-normalized/**/*.safetensors
# core-issues4.txt Section F step 6b: cycle-b2-control-v2's own merged
# tensor shards (same convention as cycle-b2 above -- targets differ,
# inputs/topology are the same real, non-regenerated data).
!data/learning-v2/cycle-b2-control-v2/tensors/**/*.safetensors
!data/learning-v2/cycle-b2-control-v2/tensors-normalized/**/*.safetensors
# core-issues3.txt Phase 10.4: the balanced supported-category OOD
# extension corpus (real, independently-generated development_holdout-only
# scenarios for EXTREME_DEMAND/TANK_STATE_SHIFT/ROUGHNESS_MISMATCH/
# FROZEN_DRIFTING_SENSOR). Raw scenario .npz arrays stay ignored, same as
# every other corpus above -- only the tensor shards are committed.
!data/learning-v2/cycle-b2-ood-extension/tensors/**/*.safetensors
!data/learning-v2/cycle-b2-ood-extension/tensors-normalized/**/*.safetensors
models/checkpoints/
experiments/cache/
experiments/runs/
experiments/registry/*.lock
experiments/jobs/*/job.lock
experiments/jobs/*/job.pid
/temp.inp
/temp.bin
/temp.rpt

# Locally generated release and browser-test artifacts. Historical submission
# evidence logs remain tracked; only transient final-head logs are ignored.
/RELEASE_MANIFEST.json
/frontend/reports/
/output/releases/
/reports/submission-readiness/jobs/*.pid
/reports/submission-readiness/jobs/final-head-playwright.log
/reports/submission-readiness/jobs/final-head-pytest.log
/reports/submission-readiness/jobs/release-path-validation.log

# M10.2 Scout refit (Level A): development-only, not-yet-promoted candidate
# checkpoints, deterministically regenerable from the frozen, hashed protocol
# (m10_2_refit_protocol.py) plus the committed training script under the
# exact commit each checkpoint_identity.json records. Per this milestone's
# "large raw checkpoints should not be committed unless the repository's
# existing artifact/LFS policy explicitly requires them" rule -- it does not
# here (unlike models/hydrocore-v4-release/model.safetensors, this is not a
# release artifact). checkpoint_identity.json (hash/provenance) stays tracked.
/reports/evaluation/hydrocore-v5/m10/m10-2-refit/checkpoints/*/model.safetensors

# M10.3A Strategist refit (Level A/B): same rationale/convention as the
# M10.2 Scout refit entry above -- development-only, not-yet-promoted
# candidate checkpoints, deterministically regenerable from the frozen,
# hashed protocol (m10_3_refit_protocol.py) plus the committed training
# scripts. checkpoint_identity.json stays tracked.
/reports/evaluation/hydrocore-v5/m10/m10-3-refit/checkpoints/*/model.safetensors

# Local final-presentation demo-clip recordings (frontend/tests/video/
# record-demo-clips.spec.ts). Large source video, regenerable by re-running
# the harness against a real running v0.2.1 release -- never committed.
/artifacts/video-recording/

# exp/candidate-conditioned-localizer-v1 (EXPERIMENTAL, NON-RELEASE): trained-
# arm checkpoints from run_experiment.py, deterministically regenerable from
# the committed script plus the fixed seed/config it records
# (reports/evaluation/candidate-conditioned-localizer-v1/run-manifest.json) --
# same not-a-release-artifact rationale as
# /experiments/graph-structural-encoder-v2/runs/ on
# exp/graph-structural-encoder-v2. The evaluation JSON/JSONL outputs under
# reports/evaluation/candidate-conditioned-localizer-v1/ ARE committed.
/experiments/candidate-conditioned-localizer-v1/runs/
